       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 5000 mg three times daily is 15 g/day, which is almost four times the usual adult maximum of 4 g/day. A single 5000 mg dose is also above the usual single-dose maximum of 1000 mg. At this dose, even with normal liver function, there is a serious risk of hepatotoxicity and acute liver failure.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **500 mg** orally three times daily (1.5 g/day)\n- **650 mg** orally three times daily (1.95 g/day)\n- **1000 mg** orally three times daily (3 g/day). This is a common regimen and stays within the 4 g/day limit.\n\nIf you really do want 5000 mg three times daily, for example because of a protocol I don't know about, tell me and I'll reconsider. Otherwise, tell me the dose you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
