      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Acetaminophen at 15 g/day is a toxic dose, and I can't think of a clinical setting where it would be appropriate. It's well into the range where acute liver injury is expected, and the 5000 mg single doses alone exceed the threshold for concern. Your confirmation doesn't change that. It could seriously harm the patient.\n\nYou can still get appropriate treatment started in these ways:\n- **Maximum standard dosing:** I can enter 1000 mg orally three times daily (3 g/day), or 1000 mg four times daily (4 g/day) if you want the ceiling.\n- **Pain not controlled by acetaminophen:** I can enter a multimodal option, such as an NSAID or other agent, if you tell me the drug and dose.\n- **Possible entry error:** If you meant 500 mg or 650 mg, give me the dose and I'll enter it right away.\n- **Unusual protocol:** If a toxicology, pharmacy, or protocol-based process calls for this dose, it should go through pharmacy verification. I'd suggest contacting the pharmacist or poison control first.\n\nWhich of these would you like?"
      }
     ],
